        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vittorio De Sica, Robert Altman, Adolfo Franci\n- Films: Shoeshine\n- Concepts: Italian neorealism, New Hollywood, Academy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- Vittorio De Sica was born on 7 July 1901 and died on 13 November 1974.\n- Vittorio De Sica was an Italian director and actor and a leading figure in the neorealist movement.\n- Robert Altman was born on February 20, 1925 and died on November 20, 2006.\n- Robert Altman was an American film director, screenwriter, and film producer.\n- Shoeshine is a 1946 Italian film directed by Vittorio De Sica.\n- Adolfo Franci was nominated for the Academy Award for Writing Original Screenplay for his work on Shoeshine.\n- Robert Altman was a five-time nominee for the Academy Award for Best Director.\n- Robert Altman was an enduring figure of the New Hollywood era.\n- Robert Altman was considered a maverick for making films with a highly naturalistic, stylized, and satirical aesthetic unlike most Hollywood films.\n- Robert Altman is consistently ranked as one of the greatest and most influential filmmakers in American cinema.",
